M32 random-route TP4 W13 NCU control/candidate comparison
Date: 2026-09-03
Both captures use profile_v4_flash_tp_local.py, one 256 MiB L2 clear before
the local pipeline, NCU cache-control=all, clock-control=none, and select only
the first route_gemm launch (W13 split-K=4).  Metric-replay timings are
diagnostic and are not headline CUDA-Graph latencies.

Metric                              Control prefetch=0   Candidate prefetch=1
Duration (us)                       127.97               125.82
Executed instructions              47,157,147           47,838,059
Registers/thread                   48                   56
Dynamic shared KiB                 21.50                21.50
Achieved occupancy (%)             53.31                53.35
One or more eligible (%)           70.19                72.11
No eligible (%)                    29.81                27.89
Warp cycles / issued instruction   12.20                11.89
DRAM throughput (%)                52.35                53.23
Compute throughput (%)             67.60                70.03

Candidate W13 duration is 1.68% lower (1.017x speedup), despite executing
1.44% more instructions.  Occupancy is unchanged.  Eligible cycles rise by
1.92 points and warp cycles per issued instruction fall 2.54%, independently
supporting the intended latency-hiding mechanism.

